<section id="about" class="about">
  <div class="container inner">
    <div class="portrait" data-reveal>
      <picture>
        <source srcset="/img/shoyeb.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img
          src="/img/shoyeb.jpg"
          width="1000"
          height="1250"
          alt="Shoyeb Akhtar"
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </picture>
    </div>

    <div class="text">
      <p class="label">About</p>
      <h2>Hi, I&rsquo;m Shoyeb.</h2>

      <p>
        I build apps for phones &mdash; the kind that earn a place on someone&rsquo;s home
        screen and get opened without thinking.
      </p>

      <p>
        What pulled me into mobile is how real it is. You write something one week, and the
        next it is running in a stranger&rsquo;s hand, on a patchy connection, on a device
        three years older than the one you tested on. There is no staging environment to
        hide behind, and I love that. It keeps the work honest.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’ve built two apps from an empty repo. The first was at a startup where I was
        part of the founding team; the second is live on the App Store and Google Play. In
        both cases, I owned the app from the first commit through the first release and
        everything that followed.
      </p>

      <p>
        The part I enjoy most is the craft. Making a list scroll smoothly on cheap hardware.
        Cutting a load time from three seconds to one. Staying with a crash until it finally
        admits what it is. These problems have real answers, and when you get one right you
        can feel the difference in your hand.
      </p>

      <p class="personal">
        Outside of work, I travel whenever I get the chance. I’d rather see a place with
        my own eyes than read about it.
      </p>

      <p class="where">
        Based in Bengaluru. Worked with teams across the globe.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
